        "comments": "The assembly daSenVulg1.hap1.1 is based on 107x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. It looks like the species used to be an allotetraploid (4n = 40), but now works as a functional diploid. HAP1 file is chromosome-level curated and contains one copy of each sub genome.",
